    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `bulkSignupWarning` flag to the owner-create flow: it is `true` when **more than 80 owners had already been created** for the same (business-day-adjusted) registration date at the moment this owner was created, and `false` otherwise. It's computed once at create time and persisted, so it reads back consistently on `GET /api/owners/{id}` (the path the acceptance test asserts against) \u2014 the same snapshot pattern the existing `namesakeCount` field uses.\n\n### Changes\n- **New pipeline step** `AssignBulkSignupWarning.java` \u2014 counts existing owners sharing the new owner's effective `registrationDate` (before the save, so the new owner isn't counted) and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. This mirrors `RequireDailyLimit`'s accumulation path (the daily hard cap is 100, so the warning band is 81\u2013100), exactly as the test's javadoc describes.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the step in between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance, so it runs after `BuildOwner` sets the effective date and before persistence.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`, column `bulk_signup_warning`) field with getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping expression coalescing a `null` stored value to `false`, guaranteeing the response is always a boolean (never null) per the \"otherwise false\" spec.\n- **`schema.sql`** for all four DBs (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column.\n\n### Verification\n- The existing `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` (fresh create \u2192 `false`) passes; full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n- I also ran a throwaway boundary test confirming both branches (81 already created \u2192 `true`; exactly 80 \u2192 `false`), then removed it and re-ran the full suite green.",
